    "message": "fix(install): rename path must not fall through to the deferred helper after success\n\nThe rename-then-reinstall path wrapped its success in try/catch and returned\nthe version; the caller's catch swallowed any post-success noise and fell\nthrough to Start-DeferredInstall, which re-staged the already-consumed wheel\nand failed with Copy-Item. Live test caught it: the install actually succeeded\n(5.3.2 live with launchers open) but the run ended in a noisy fallback error.\n\nInvoke-RenameThenReinstall now returns a boolean ($true on success, $false only\nwhen the rename itself is refused) and the caller short-circuits on $true.\nWheel temp cleanup moved to a finally around the whole running-launcher branch\nso every path (rename success, deferral fallback) cleans up once.\n\nVersion 5.3.2 unchanged (same release, installer-only correction within it).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
